# config/extensions/Kconfig — Extensions: what a use adds to the common base
#
# An extension adds to the base kernel and never changes it. Its kernel side is
# the crates it links and the effect providers it installs through the contract
# in crates/core/ext-api (its Manifest); its user side is its ring-3 services.
# A preset picks extensions by default; a manual choice wins. An extension
# pulls what it needs with `imply`, never `select`.

menu "Extensions"

config EXT_ROBOT
    bool "Robot: motors, sensors, safety envelope and the brain link"
    default y if PRESET_ROBOT
    imply BOARD_IO
    help
      The robot extension (USE_ROBOT, kernel feature `use-robot`): the
      crates under crates/domains/robot (behavior and the brain link, the
      motor control loop and its per-robot-type envelope, IMU / barometer /
      GPS / AHRS, flight, navigation, telemetry, the ESC and RC drivers),
      the board's sensors (BOARD_IO) and the camera frame ring. Its effect
      provider (`azos_safety_core::actuation::ROBOT`) stops the wheels, the
      ESC and the payload whenever the e-stop latches. Off, none of it is
      linked (tools/lint/profile_cut_lint.py, the `robot` cut).

endmenu # Extensions
